        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d59299b9-d156-5fed-bd85-1b078d3c3aae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Zoltan Korda, Robert Wise, Carl Boese, Gustav Fröhlich, Evelyn Holt, Lissy Arna\n- Places: United States, Hollywood\n- Industries: American film industry\n- Films: Citizen Kane, The Eleven Devils, West Side Story, The Sound of Music, The Sand Pebbles\n- Awards: Academy Awards, Best Director, Best Picture, Best Film Editing\n\nFacts:\n- The Eleven Devils is a 1927 German silent film directed by Zoltan Korda and Carl Boese and starring Gustav Fröhlich, Evelyn Holt, and Lissy Arna.\n- Robert Wise was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Film Editing for Citizen Kane in 1941.\n- Zoltan Korda and another person moved to the United States in 1940, settling in Hollywood and entering the American film industry.\n- Robert Wise won the Academy Awards for Best Director and Best Picture for West Side Story in 1961.\n- Robert Wise won the Academy Awards for Best Director and Best Picture for The Sound of Music in 1965.\n- Robert Wise directed and produced The Sand Pebbles in 1966, and the film was nominated for Best Picture.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "dbe1f8f5-bdd6-55cf-baaf-b6ebb66f87ec",
        "text": "Page: Zoltan Korda. Sentence: They both moved to the United States in 1940 to Hollywood and the American film industry.\nPage: Robert Wise. Sentence: He won Academy Awards for Best Director and Best Picture for both \"West Side Story\" (1961) and \"The Sound of Music\" (1965).\nPage: Robert Wise. Sentence: He was also nominated for Best Film Editing for \"Citizen Kane\" (1941) and directed and produced \"The Sand Pebbles\" (1966), which was nominated for Best Picture.\nPage: The Eleven Devils. Sentence: The Eleven Devils (German: Die elf Teufel) is a 1927 German silent film directed by Zoltan Korda and Carl Boese and starring Gustav Fröhlich, Evelyn Holt and Lissy Arna.",
